    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>min</mi><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"}\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></math>. If&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math> is the number of points, where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi></math> is not differentiable and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math>&nbsp;is the number of points, where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi></math> is not continuous, then the ordered pair <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is equal to"
